  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements: one is labelled as &ldquo;Assertion A&rdquo; and the other is labelled as &ldquo;Reason R&rdquo;</p><p>Assertion A : In the complex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CO</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>4</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CO</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>5</mn></msub></math>, the metals have zero oxidation state.</p><p>Reason R : Low oxidation states are found when a complex has ligands capable of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi></math>-donor character in addition to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#963;</mi></math>-bonding.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "uzj39",
      "text": "A is correct but R is not correct",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2ttTk",
      "text": "A is not correct but R is correct",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "td1V1",
      "text": "Both A and R are correct but R is NOT the correct explanation of A",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3N1Q3",
      "text": "Both A and R are correct and R is the correct explanation of A",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The ligand carbon monoxide has no charge, hence metals have zero oxidation state in both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CO</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>4</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CO</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>5</mn></msub></math>. Low oxidation states are found when a complex has ligands capable of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi></math>-acceptor character in addition to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#963;</mi></math>-bonding.</p><p>In the complexes,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CO</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Fe</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CO</mi></mfenced><mn>5</mn></msub></math>, the ligand&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CO</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mo>-</mo></math>acceptor character in addition to the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>bonding</mi></math>.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
